In our discussion, James sought a punchy title for his paper "Reductions in economic outcomes due to climate change today," which had attracted interest from Nature. He needed to incorporate "systematic review" due to a reviewer's requirement without making the title too clunky. After considering Nature's preference against colons, I suggested "Systematic Review of Economic Losses Due to Climate Change Today," but he clarified that it was based on a systematic review rather than a review of all economic losses. We then explored alternative titles and eventually refined it to "Economic Outcomes from Climate Change Today Informed by a Systematic Review," which fulfilled clarity and punctuation requirements.
